│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ full_greedy_multistart                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ The current greedy only samples 10 random candidate transactions per step and sometimes   │
│                          │ picks a purely random one (sample_rate), which is noisy and myopic. A better approach: at │
│                          │ each step, evaluate **every** remaining transaction by computing the makespan of the      │
│                          │ partial schedule extended with that transaction, and pick the best one (full greedy       │
│                          │ lookahead). Since greedy from a single start can get stuck in local optima, we run many   │
│                          │ random restarts (each starting from a different first transaction) and keep the best      │
│                          │ complete schedule found. This directly optimizes the actual makespan metric via           │
│                          │ `get_opt_seq_cost` at each decision, avoiding heuristic proxies, and the multistart       │
│                          │ provides diversification. To reduce cost, we first compute per-transaction times once,    │
│                          │ and use a time budget so the search terminates reliably.                                  │
│ num_applied              │ 1                                                                                         │
