│ patch_description        │ The current code runs a single greedy pass with sampling, which is highly noisy. A much   │
│                          │ better approach is:                                                                       │
│                          │ 1. Run the greedy-with-sampling construction many times (randomized restarts), since each │
│                          │ run is cheap and gives a diverse pool of schedules.                                       │
│                          │ 2. Improve the best candidates with a local search: try moving a transaction to a         │
│                          │ different position (insertion neighborhood) and swapping pairs, accepting improvements in │
│                          │ makespan. This directly optimizes the actual objective (`get_opt_seq_cost`) rather than   │
│                          │ heuristics.                                                                               │
│                          │ Since `get_opt_seq_cost` evaluates the true makespan, a hill-climbing refinement over     │
│                          │ insertion/swap moves — repeated over multiple restarts within a time budget — will        │
│                          │ systematically reduce makespan compared to a single noisy greedy run. Time-budgeted       │
│                          │ multistart ensures we use whatever compute is available and always return the best        │
│                          │ schedule found.                                                                           │
