│                          │ (beam width k), expand each beam by all remaining transactions, keep the k best by        │
│                          │ incremental makespan cost. This explores the ordering space far more broadly than the     │
│                          │ current sampled greedy, which only ever considers one random candidate per step and often │
│                          │ locks in bad early choices. Beam search with full expansion avoids sampling noise and     │
│                          │ keeps multiple promising orderings alive, yielding much lower makespans. To keep it       │
│                          │ tractable, use a lookahead-limited expansion and randomized restarts to escape local      │
│                          │ optima.                                                                                   │
