│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ greedy_plus_local_search_restarts                                                         │
│ patch_description        │ The current version only runs a single greedy pass (the outer restart loop was removed,   │
│                          │ sample_rate=1.0). The prior best program showed that multiple randomized greedy restarts  │
│                          │ significantly improve makespan (2832 vs a single run's 2801 baseline). I propose          │
│                          │ restoring multi-restart randomized greedy (30 restarts), but adding a 2-opt style local   │
│                          │ search: after each greedy solution, repeatedly try swapping adjacent pairs and moving a   │
│                          │ transaction to a different position; if makespan improves, keep it. This refines each     │
│                          │ greedy solution beyond its myopic construction, typically shaving several units of        │
│                          │ makespan per workload. We also sample more candidates when few remain (cheap              │
│                          │ evaluations), and keep the best overall.                                                  │
