│ patch_name               │ beam_search_time_budgeted                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Gen 10 showed that pure beam search (289 makespan) beats variants with local search       │
│                          │ layered on top (292), because local search consumes wall-clock budget that is better      │
│                          │ spent on more beam search restarts with larger beams. This rewrite drops the local search │
│                          │ entirely and instead converts all spare compute into beam search restarts: it keeps       │
│                          │ running beam searches (with randomized seed transactions and full lookahead expansion     │
│                          │ over remaining transactions, evaluated by actual `get_opt_seq_cost`) in a loop until a    │
│                          │ 25-second wall-clock budget is exhausted. Each restart's beam members are recorded as     │
│                          │ candidates, and the best full schedule found is returned. Since beam search greedily      │
│                          │ builds schedules by actual makespan cost, more restarts with wider beams directly sample  │
│                          │ the space of good prefix orderings, which is the dimension that demonstrably improves the │
│                          │ makespan.                                                                                 │
