│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ beam_search_multistart                                                                    │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the randomized greedy sampling with a beam search over partial schedules. At each │
│                          │ step, for each beam candidate, evaluate ALL remaining transactions by their single-step   │
│                          │ lookahead makespan (computed with get_opt_seq_cost on the extended prefix), keep the      │
│                          │ top-k lowest-cost extensions, and run many randomized restarts (each seeded with a        │
│                          │ different starting transaction plus randomized tie-breaking) to escape local optima. Beam │
│                          │ search with full one-step lookahead is fundamentally stronger than random sampling        │
│                          │ because it systematically explores the best extensions rather than sampling a few random  │
│                          │ ones, while multiple restarts with shuffled seeds provide diversity.                      │
