│ patch_type               │ full                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ adaptive_beam_plus_polish                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ Builds on the beam-search framework but adds: (1) adaptive beam width — wide early (where │
│                          │ pruning error compounds most), narrowing as partial schedules grow; (2) a wall-clock      │
│                          │ budget (~25s) so beam width and restarts scale to actual runtime rather than fixed        │
│                          │ counts; (3) diversified seeds per restart; and (4) a final insertion-move polish          │
│                          │ (relocate each transaction to its best position) applied to the best schedule found,      │
│                          │ which reliably shaves off remaining makespan that beam pruning leaves behind. The key     │
│                          │ insight from prior programs is that actual-cost evaluation at each step beats heuristics, │
│                          │ and that greedy+local-search and beam search are complementary — beam explores broadly,   │
│                          │ polish exploits deeply.                                                                   │
