│ patch_name               │ beam_greedy_sa_hybrid                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ This crossover combines the strongest elements from both programs: (1) the beam search    │
│                          │ with adaptive beam width from the current program (best-scoring phase-1 constructor), (2) │
│                          │ the fast full-lookahead greedy with randomized multistart from the inspiration program    │
│                          │ used to generate additional diverse candidate schedules cheaply within the phase-1        │
│                          │ budget, and (3) the time-budgeted simulated annealing with greedy-insertion               │
│                          │ intensification for phase-2 refinement. Reasoning: beam search explores broadly but each  │
│                          │ restart uses random seeds; the greedy multistart cheaply produces good, diverse           │
│                          │ candidates (with tie-breaking for diversification) that seed SA from different basins,    │
│                          │ improving escape from local minima. SA from multiple starting points with intensification │
│                          │ sweeps has proven to drive the makespan down; feeding it both beam candidates and greedy  │
│                          │ candidates increases the chance one lands near a global optimum.                          │
