│ patch_description        │ Key changes over the current program: (1) Beam restarts are now seeded with a             │
│                          │ heuristic-plus-random mix — the top-2 transactions by single-transaction cost plus one    │
│                          │ random pick — instead of {0, rand, rand}. This injects the deterministic lookahead        │
│                          │ strength early in construction, which the prior recommendation identified as high-value.  │
│                          │ (2) Beam width and restart count are raised (more of the 40% construction budget spent    │
│                          │ productively). (3) Randomized greedy uses full lookahead (sample_rate=1) more often,      │
│                          │ matching the strong full-lookahead greedy. (4) ILS keeps more top candidates (6), uses    │
│                          │ first-improvement insertion/swap (accept immediately, faster descent), and deduplicates   │
│                          │ by cost+tuple. (5) Slightly larger time budget utilization with tighter deadline checks.  │
│                          │ These parameter changes reduce wasted evaluations on bad seeds and concentrate search on  │
│                          │ the most promising basins, lowering makespan.                                             │
