│ patch_description        │ The beam search currently uses purely random starting transactions. Since the first       │
│                          │ transactions placed have outsized impact on the final makespan (they determine the        │
│                          │ baseline cost before conflicts accumulate), seeding beam restarts with the cheapest       │
│                          │ single-transaction candidates gives the beam a strong deterministic foundation, while     │
│                          │ random seeds still provide diversity to escape local optima. I compute each transaction's │
│                          │ standalone cost via `get_opt_seq_cost()`, take the top-2 cheapest as seeds, and add a few │
│                          │ random seeds for exploration. This merges the deterministic lookahead strength that made  │
│                          │ greedy effective with restart diversity, and it's a minimal change to the `starts`        │
│                          │ construction. I also bump the number of random restarts from 4 to 5 since seeds are now   │
│                          │ more informative and low-cost.                                                            │
