│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ replace_sa_with_ils_oropt_moves                                                           │
│ patch_description        │ Prior generations showed that simulated-annealing refinement (current Phase 2) and        │
│                          │ iterated local search (ILS) both plateau at makespan 275, while plain insertion/swap      │
│                          │ neighborhoods are too weak to escape local optima. The literature on sequencing problems  │
│                          │ (e.g., Job-Shop / TSP local search) consistently shows that adding **or-opt block moves   │
│                          │ (segment reinsertion of 2–3 consecutive transactions)** and **2-opt segment reversals**   │
│                          │ dramatically enriches the neighborhood: a single or-opt move changes the relative order   │
│                          │ of many transaction pairs at once, which pure insertion/swap cannot reach in one step.    │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Plan:                                                                                     │
│                          │ 1. Replace the Phase-2 SA loop with an ILS framework: a deterministic first-improvement   │
│                          │ local search over four neighborhoods (insertion, swap, or-opt blocks of size 2–3, 2-opt   │
│                          │ reversal), each with per-candidate deadline checks so the time budget is respected.       │
│                          │ 2. After each local-search convergence, apply a random segment-shuffle perturbation and   │
│                          │ re-optimize, keeping improvements (classic ILS "restart from perturbed incumbent" scheme, │
│                          │ which outperforms pure SA because it never wanders away from good basins).                │
│                          │ 3. Keep beam-search construction and greedy candidates from Phase 1 unchanged, but also   │
│                          │ add cheap randomized greedy constructions to diversify the seed pool for ILS.             │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ This merges the proven ILS framework with the richer move set, which should push makespan │
│                          │ below the current 275 plateau.                                                            │
