│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ ils_with_or_opt_moves                                                                     │
│ patch_description        │ Replace the beam search with a hybrid: a fast greedy nearest-neighbor construction        │
│                          │ (picking the transaction that increases makespan the least at each step, with several     │
│                          │ restarts from different seeds), followed by an Iterated Local Search using insertion      │
│                          │ (or-1), swap, and or-opt segment moves (blocks of length 2–3) with restart perturbation.  │
│                          │ This evaluates actual makespan via `get_opt_seq_cost` on full sequences, which is         │
│                          │ expensive, so local search only computes costs on full candidate sequences but keeps      │
│                          │ candidate generation cheap (O(n) per move type). Greedy construction gives a strong       │
│                          │ starting solution quickly; ILS with rich neighborhoods (or-opt blocks of 2–3 proven       │
│                          │ valuable in prior gens) then improves it. A time-budget-free iteration cap scaled by n    │
│                          │ keeps runtime reasonable.                                                                 │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Reasoning step-by-step: (1) greedy construction picks at each step the txn minimizing     │
│                          │ actual makespan increment — much faster than beam search while nearly as good; (2)        │
│                          │ multiple greedy restarts from random seeds diversify; (3) local search with insertion +   │
│                          │ swap + or-opt(2,3) removes ordering inefficiencies; (4) perturbation (random 3-swap)      │
│                          │ escapes local optima; (5) accepting only improving full solutions guarantees no           │
│                          │ regression, and we track the global best across all restarts.                             │
