│ Field                    │ Value                                                                                     │
├──────────────────────────┼───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│ patch_type               │ diff                                                                                      │
│ patch_name               │ add_lns_and_cost_clustered_seeds                                                          │
│ patch_description        │ The current program regressed (3584 vs the best 3787.88). Two targeted fixes based on     │
│                          │ what worked in prior generations:                                                         │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 1. **Cost-clustered seed selection for beam search**: Prior generations showed the top-2  │
│                          │ cheapest single-txn seeds plus random seeds beat always using txn 0. Instead of always    │
│                          │ seeding with txn 0, group transactions by cost quantile and pick one seed per quantile    │
│                          │ bucket, rotating across restarts. This systematically covers different seed basins rather │
│                          │ than repeatedly concentrating on the same seed.                                           │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ 2. **Add a Large Neighborhood Search (LNS) ruin-and-recreate phase**: The generation that │
│                          │ achieved 3745 used LNS after SA, removing a contiguous block of transactions and greedily │
│                          │ reinserting each at its best position. This is a powerful escape from local optima that   │
│                          │ single insertion/swap SA moves cannot reach, and directly evaluates real makespan via     │
│                          │ `get_opt_seq_cost`. Adding it back on top of the current SA phase should recover and      │
│                          │ improve on the best known score.                                                          │
│                          │                                                                                           │
│                          │ Reasoning step-by-step:                                                                   │
│                          │ - Construction phase (greedy + diverse beam) yields good starting schedules.              │
│                          │ - SA with insertion intensification refines them locally.                                 │
│                          │ - LNS then perturbs structurally (removes 2-6 consecutive txns and optimally reinserts    │
│                          │ each), which explores a much larger neighborhood per evaluation and often finds improving │
│                          │ moves SA misses. Sideways acceptance (30% on equal cost) adds diversification.            │
│                          │ - Budget: LNS gets the remaining time up to the 28s wall clock, which was previously      │
│                          │ wasted or underused.                                                                      │
