│ patch_name               │ hybrid_greedy_beam_sa_lns                                                                 │
│ patch_description        │ The best prior programs reached makespan 261 by combining: (1) cheap, diverse             │
│                          │ full-lookahead greedy constructions (randomized tie-breaking, sampled candidate sets),    │
│                          │ (2) a diversity-preserving depth-adaptive beam search (top width-2 by cost plus 2         │
│                          │ children with differing last transactions, avoiding prefix collapse), (3) simulated       │
│                          │ annealing with greedy insertion intensification on the top candidates, and (4) an LNS     │
│                          │ ruin-and-recreate phase on the incumbent. I combine all four phases with a 28s budget     │
│                          │ split roughly 15% greedy, 50% beam, 75% SA, and the remainder LNS. The greedy phase       │
│                          │ provides diverse, cheap seeds whose diversity drives beam and SA success; beam search     │
│                          │ with diversity-preserving pruning avoids converging on identical prefixes; SA with        │
│                          │ insertion sweeps escapes local optima; LNS block reinsertion provides large-neighborhood  │
│                          │ improvements. All moves are evaluated by actual makespan via get_opt_seq_cost, per the    │
│                          │ task guidance that heuristics like length/write-count don't correlate with makespan.      │
